00:00:39.889 --> 00:00:43.021
- I think that financial
success is not success.

00:00:43.021 --> 00:00:46.276
You know to me, when people say

00:00:46.276 --> 00:00:48.299
for example I showed Pan's Labyrinth

00:00:48.299 --> 00:00:51.304
and somebody said why don't
you take out the violence?

00:00:51.304 --> 00:00:52.584
And it was very well-meaning.

00:00:52.584 --> 00:00:53.581
Why don't you take out the violence

00:00:53.581 --> 00:00:56.019
so you can reach a wider audience?

00:00:56.019 --> 00:00:58.034
It's because I don't
want a wider audience.

00:00:58.034 --> 00:01:00.489
I want the audience for the movie.

00:01:00.489 --> 00:01:03.647
Each movie has an audience, that's it.

00:01:03.647 --> 00:01:07.392
It's not going to get more
or less if you, with it,

00:01:07.392 --> 00:01:08.634
if you amputate it,

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.368
if you cripple it, that's all you do.

00:01:11.368 --> 00:01:13.322
You know, people dream
of a bigger audience

00:01:13.322 --> 00:01:16.848
and they go, well, you
know, but is it the movie?

00:01:16.848 --> 00:01:20.015
If in order to make more people happy,

00:01:20.912 --> 00:01:24.857
you know Cinderella doesn't
get the prince at the end,

00:01:24.857 --> 00:01:28.722
I don't know, it's not the same tale.

00:01:28.722 --> 00:01:31.687
As much as I like the Disney films

00:01:31.687 --> 00:01:34.485
of the renaissance of animation, I can't.

00:01:34.485 --> 00:01:36.018
Every time I see The Little Mermaid

00:01:36.018 --> 00:01:39.118
I think, but she dies in the book.

00:01:39.118 --> 00:01:40.702
She dies at the end.

00:01:40.702 --> 00:01:42.555
That's what made it beautiful,

00:01:42.555 --> 00:01:44.489
that the prince was ultimately so stupid.

00:01:44.489 --> 00:01:46.978
And I understand they are
reaching a wider audience,

00:01:46.978 --> 00:01:50.179
but is it the tale that Hans
Christian Andersen wrote?

00:01:50.179 --> 00:01:51.738
No way.

00:01:51.738 --> 00:01:54.819
It's a different movie,
it's a different tale.

00:01:54.819 --> 00:01:59.231
So if you're asking me, was
Little Mermaid successful

00:01:59.231 --> 00:02:04.021
as a film, I say it was,

00:02:04.021 --> 00:02:07.127
but it wasn't the tale.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.988
It's a great, I love those films,

00:02:08.988 --> 00:02:10.799
I really think they're
beautifully constructed,

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:12.828
but it's not the tale.

00:02:12.828 --> 00:02:16.382
So Pan's Labyrinth without the violence,

00:02:16.382 --> 00:02:18.203
is not Pan's Labyrinth.

00:02:18.203 --> 00:02:22.405
Is, I don't know, it's a
fantasy like Harry Potter

00:02:22.405 --> 00:02:25.815
or Narnia or any other fantasy film.

00:02:25.815 --> 00:02:28.725
- Greatness is a different
definition to different people.

00:02:28.725 --> 00:02:30.901
Greatness to me, is,

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:33.937
when I land that fakey ab
cab hill, on my skateboard,

00:02:33.937 --> 00:02:35.226
or some.

00:02:35.226 --> 00:02:38.129
Greatness is the song
I recorded last week.

00:02:38.129 --> 00:02:41.097
Somebody might not find that
great, but it's great to me,

00:02:41.097 --> 00:02:42.816
and that's all that matters,

00:02:42.816 --> 00:02:44.482
what the I think, in my head.

00:02:44.482 --> 00:02:47.126
As long as I like it,
that's all that matters.

00:02:47.126 --> 00:02:51.320
Greatness to me, is finally
getting my video on MTV.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.837
It's on there now, and I'm,

00:02:53.837 --> 00:02:57.002
I'm happy I finally got my, on MTV.

00:02:57.002 --> 00:02:59.233
Some people might think that's
selling out or whatever,

00:02:59.233 --> 00:03:00.635
but I don't really give a.

00:03:00.635 --> 00:03:03.138
That's great to me, I'm proud of myself.

00:03:03.138 --> 00:03:05.386
I've been wanting that
since I was seven years old,

00:03:05.386 --> 00:03:07.282
and I finally got that,

00:03:07.282 --> 00:03:09.287
and hard work pays the off.

00:03:09.287 --> 00:03:10.958
- [Interviewer] At the end
of our session yesterday,

00:03:10.958 --> 00:03:15.462
you said thank you to Scott
for reviving my career,

00:03:15.462 --> 00:03:17.649
and I don't know if that's in jest,

00:03:17.649 --> 00:03:20.766
because I've never had
the impression that you,

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:23.023
you're desperate for box office,

00:03:23.023 --> 00:03:25.479
but you choose--
- I'm jagging for it.

00:03:25.479 --> 00:03:29.199
It's been my, it's been the thrust of my,

00:03:29.199 --> 00:03:33.294
of my interest since day
one, when I was about 19.

00:03:33.294 --> 00:03:34.733
Yeah, that's all I care about.

00:03:34.733 --> 00:03:36.783
20 years of failures will do that to you.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:39.927
- [Interviewer] But, on a different level,

00:03:39.927 --> 00:03:43.086
why do you say that, and how do you feel

00:03:43.086 --> 00:03:46.222
when you choose a role that
ends up satisfying you,

00:03:46.222 --> 00:03:48.785
that this one clearly did?

00:03:48.785 --> 00:03:51.329
- Well you know, for
me, with every character

00:03:51.329 --> 00:03:55.219
that you play, you know, as long as you've

00:03:55.219 --> 00:03:58.822
reached that, you've arrived at that place

00:03:58.822 --> 00:04:02.624
where you believe is the right place to be

00:04:02.624 --> 00:04:04.124
for the character,

00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:06.072
and

00:04:07.465 --> 00:04:09.950
if you feel that you've
done service to the,

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:13.474
to the director, to
yourself, to the author,

00:04:13.474 --> 00:04:15.225
then, to me,

00:04:15.225 --> 00:04:17.694
to me that's a success.

00:04:17.694 --> 00:04:19.527
Box office is kind of,

00:04:20.537 --> 00:04:21.794
you know, that's something else,

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.228
that's certainly none of my business,

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:24.061
you know what I mean?

00:04:24.061 --> 00:04:26.403
Once I'm wrapped on a film, it's just,

00:04:26.403 --> 00:04:29.364
say goodbye to the character
and then move forward.

00:04:29.364 --> 00:04:32.516
- Everyone in this room wants to make it,

00:04:32.516 --> 00:04:37.123
but I question how you
would recognize making it.

00:04:37.123 --> 00:04:38.294
What is making it?

00:04:38.294 --> 00:04:40.460
Well, what do you want to be?

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.569
Who in here wants a record deal?

00:04:42.569 --> 00:04:44.568
Would it be nice, it'd be nice
to have a record deal, right?

00:04:44.568 --> 00:04:45.904
We want a record deal.

00:04:45.904 --> 00:04:47.863
Okay, well what does a
record deal look like?

00:04:47.863 --> 00:04:49.843
What does making it look like?

00:04:49.843 --> 00:04:52.357
Do you want to sell a million
copies, two million copies?

00:04:52.357 --> 00:04:54.960
Well, okay, let's say,
selling two million copies

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.842
is like selling 10 million
copies, 10 years ago.

00:04:57.842 --> 00:04:59.336
So let's say you say to yourself,

00:04:59.336 --> 00:05:01.445
my expectation is that
I want to be an artist,

00:05:01.445 --> 00:05:02.532
and I want to put records out,

00:05:02.532 --> 00:05:04.264
and I want to sell millions of copies.

00:05:04.264 --> 00:05:07.244
If that's your expectation, great.

00:05:07.244 --> 00:05:10.905
Then, you sort of skip straight
to another questionnaire,

00:05:10.905 --> 00:05:12.878
you know, okay, if you answered yes to,

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:14.477
do I want to be a pop star, do I want to

00:05:14.477 --> 00:05:16.915
make music for as many people as possible,

00:05:16.915 --> 00:05:18.776
now you have to

00:05:18.776 --> 00:05:21.972
sort of change your game
to fit the expectation.

00:05:21.972 --> 00:05:23.626
You now have to wonder about,

00:05:23.626 --> 00:05:26.062
is your song shorter than four minutes?

00:05:26.062 --> 00:05:28.138
Do you get to your chorus fast enough?

00:05:28.138 --> 00:05:30.860
These are things you
have to absolutely do,

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.840
and you also have to compromise,

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.507
and you also have to

00:05:35.656 --> 00:05:37.635
play the game, you know,

00:05:37.635 --> 00:05:39.693
and by defining your expectations,

00:05:39.693 --> 00:05:42.886
if you decide that you
want to be a pop star,

00:05:42.886 --> 00:05:44.291
that's not a dirty word,

00:05:44.291 --> 00:05:47.103
it just means, pop just means popular.

00:05:47.103 --> 00:05:49.578
Frank Sinatra was a pop star.

00:05:49.578 --> 00:05:51.748
Jimi Hendrix was a pop star.

00:05:51.748 --> 00:05:53.251
Lots of people were pop stars.

00:05:53.251 --> 00:05:54.230
What kind of pop star?

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:55.846
Lots of people are jazz musicians.

00:05:55.846 --> 00:05:57.122
What kind of jazz musician?

00:05:57.122 --> 00:06:00.177
You can be, you can define
the genre any way you want.

00:06:00.177 --> 00:06:01.892
So if you said you want to be a pop star,

00:06:01.892 --> 00:06:04.221
then you have to look at your songs.

00:06:04.221 --> 00:06:05.836
There's also people here

00:06:05.836 --> 00:06:08.980
who are a little dishonest about
what they really want to be,

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.172
and I think if you want to be famous,

00:06:11.172 --> 00:06:13.713
if you want to make music for
as many people as possible,

00:06:13.713 --> 00:06:15.818
just come out and say it.

00:06:15.818 --> 00:06:17.724
Don't say, oh I want to be indie;

00:06:17.724 --> 00:06:19.764
I'm just going to be
an independent artist,

00:06:19.764 --> 00:06:23.187
and really secretly wish that
you wanted to be a pop star,

00:06:23.187 --> 00:06:26.584
because, from the very
beginning, it's disingenuous.

00:06:26.584 --> 00:06:27.545
There's nothing wrong with saying

00:06:27.545 --> 00:06:29.811
I want to play music for
as many people as possible

00:06:29.811 --> 00:06:31.724
without compromising the things

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:33.451
that I have to be as an artist,

00:06:33.451 --> 00:06:35.316
and that's what I've done.

00:06:35.316 --> 00:06:37.074
Sony Music doesn't come into the studio

00:06:37.074 --> 00:06:40.046
when I'm making a record, but I also know

00:06:40.046 --> 00:06:42.407
what's going to be a hit,
or what stands the chance

00:06:42.407 --> 00:06:44.423
of being a hit, and what just doesn't,

00:06:44.423 --> 00:06:47.640
and it's a level of honesty with yourself

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:50.568
that you have to have before
you hand your music out

00:06:50.568 --> 00:06:52.236
to anybody else.

00:06:52.236 --> 00:06:55.141
So that's sort of what I want
to say about expectations.

00:06:55.141 --> 00:06:59.541
If you only recognize
success as a record deal

00:06:59.541 --> 00:07:01.949
and a big fat Publisher's Clearing House,

00:07:01.949 --> 00:07:04.102
oversized, Tiger Woods check,

00:07:04.102 --> 00:07:06.603
and a dinner and then going
to the top of the roof

00:07:06.603 --> 00:07:10.107
and screaming, I made it,

00:07:10.107 --> 00:07:13.118
most of you will be stunning failures.

00:07:13.118 --> 00:07:14.721
- Well if you had to give someone

00:07:14.721 --> 00:07:17.058
who's recently graduating from our program

00:07:17.058 --> 00:07:18.923
a piece of advice, what would you say?

00:07:18.923 --> 00:07:20.920
- I would say to

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:24.612
learn and to execute
on your unique vision.

00:07:24.612 --> 00:07:26.405
Define success for yourself;

00:07:26.405 --> 00:07:28.040
figure out what that means to you.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.941
Don't get taken over

00:07:30.941 --> 00:07:33.712
by the world's definition of
success, or your family's,

00:07:33.712 --> 00:07:34.998
or what your friends are doing,

00:07:34.998 --> 00:07:37.847
or what anyone says, that equals success.

00:07:37.847 --> 00:07:39.665
Once you can get clear on that vision,

00:07:39.665 --> 00:07:41.309
then you need to create a plan

00:07:41.309 --> 00:07:44.196
to make that come to
life, and to prioritize.

00:07:44.196 --> 00:07:46.899
I think one of the biggest
tragedies of our time

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:49.858
is, I hear so many people
from every walk of life,

00:07:49.858 --> 00:07:53.281
health coaches all over,
feeling so overwhelmed,

00:07:53.281 --> 00:07:56.748
and overworked, and there's
so much that they can do

00:07:56.748 --> 00:07:57.876
that they feel paralyzed.

00:07:57.876 --> 00:07:59.222
Well, I don't know what to do first,

00:07:59.222 --> 00:08:01.492
or what, how do I make all of this happen?

00:08:01.492 --> 00:08:03.991
And I think that we all need
to take a few steps back

00:08:03.991 --> 00:08:06.910
and start to get clear on
our own vision for success,

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:09.879
and then actually prioritize
making that come to life,

00:08:09.879 --> 00:08:12.778
'cause then it gives you such
clarity and such freedom,

00:08:12.778 --> 00:08:14.166
and all of that static,

00:08:14.166 --> 00:08:16.225
and the overwhelm, starts to fall away.

00:08:16.225 --> 00:08:18.439
- I define success two ways.

00:08:18.439 --> 00:08:22.944
One, what I do here at the firm,

00:08:22.944 --> 00:08:25.323
the impact that I create for my clients,

00:08:25.323 --> 00:08:27.475
the impact that I create
for the partnership,

00:08:27.475 --> 00:08:29.206
now the new role that I have,

00:08:29.206 --> 00:08:30.968
the legacy that I leave.

00:08:30.968 --> 00:08:33.510
That is one way that
I will define success.

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:35.009
You know, I'm not a great cricketer.

00:08:35.009 --> 00:08:36.602
I love cricket, I wish I was

00:08:36.602 --> 00:08:39.045
as good as Sachin Tendulkar, I'm not.

00:08:39.045 --> 00:08:40.855
This is my life's work;

00:08:40.855 --> 00:08:44.488
what I do here is my life's
work, it will define me,

00:08:44.488 --> 00:08:47.035
and the second thing that will define me

00:08:47.035 --> 00:08:49.260
is what my 11-year-old son thinks of me

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.622
when he becomes a man.

00:08:51.622 --> 00:08:55.095
These are the two things
that define success for me,

00:08:55.095 --> 00:08:58.094
and in that is a little bit of a conundrum

00:08:58.094 --> 00:09:00.755
because I love what I do,

00:09:00.755 --> 00:09:02.950
it is, as I said, my life's work,

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:05.794
I love my son more than I love myself,

00:09:05.794 --> 00:09:08.382
and there's a constant tug.

00:09:08.382 --> 00:09:10.235
There isn't enough hours in the day

00:09:10.235 --> 00:09:12.691
to be able to do both extremely well,

00:09:12.691 --> 00:09:14.631
and so that is my challenge.

00:09:14.631 --> 00:09:18.014
- How do you define success for you?

00:09:18.014 --> 00:09:20.188
What is success to you?

00:09:20.188 --> 00:09:23.147
- I guess success is when,
is when people are listening,

00:09:23.147 --> 00:09:25.756
and there's some measurable change in,

00:09:25.756 --> 00:09:28.033
in consciousness, worldwide, even if it's,

00:09:28.033 --> 00:09:30.641
even if the needle barely moves, you know.

00:09:30.641 --> 00:09:32.923
I think that if you're communicating ideas

00:09:32.923 --> 00:09:35.747
and telling stories, if the feedback,

00:09:35.747 --> 00:09:38.012
if the feedback is that those,

00:09:38.012 --> 00:09:40.384
that those seeds are
landing on fertile soil,

00:09:40.384 --> 00:09:41.852
that's success.

00:09:41.852 --> 00:09:43.922
I think, you know, I would say I felt that

00:09:43.922 --> 00:09:46.322
even more with Avatar than with Titanic.

00:09:46.322 --> 00:09:50.047
Titanic, we definitely moved
people for a couple of hours,

00:09:50.047 --> 00:09:52.873
and they cried, and then they left,

00:09:52.873 --> 00:09:54.455
and that was that, you know?

00:09:54.455 --> 00:09:57.540
Avatar is a different story,
because it lingered with them,

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.980
and, you know, dare I say maybe even,

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:03.479
to some tiny, tiny degree,
may influence their

00:10:03.479 --> 00:10:05.311
perspective on how we're behaving

00:10:05.311 --> 00:10:07.081
with respect to the natural world,

00:10:07.081 --> 00:10:10.609
and basically the destruction
that we're causing.

00:10:10.609 --> 00:10:13.109
- Define success for yourself.

00:10:14.996 --> 00:10:17.163
You already like that one?

00:10:18.058 --> 00:10:20.196
Define success for yourself,
now check this out.

00:10:20.196 --> 00:10:22.669
I'm in, south of New Orleans,

00:10:22.669 --> 00:10:26.488
a few years ago, and I
went to a voodoo shop,

00:10:26.488 --> 00:10:29.947
and they had this wooden
partition against the wall,

00:10:29.947 --> 00:10:32.077
with these columns, and in these columns,

00:10:32.077 --> 00:10:35.782
were all these vials of
these magic potions, right?

00:10:35.782 --> 00:10:37.520
And the headings above each potion,

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:40.574
defining what they would
give you, were things like

00:10:40.574 --> 00:10:44.843
fertility, health, family, legal help,

00:10:44.843 --> 00:10:48.260
energy, forgiveness, money.

00:10:49.427 --> 00:10:51.844
Guess which column was empty.

00:10:52.957 --> 00:10:55.014
Money.

00:10:55.014 --> 00:10:56.885
Let's admit it,

00:10:56.885 --> 00:11:00.187
money is king today, it's
what makes the world go round,

00:11:00.187 --> 00:11:02.360
it is success, the more we have,

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:05.193
the more successful we are, right?

00:11:06.406 --> 00:11:09.326
Now, I would argue that
our cultural values

00:11:09.326 --> 00:11:11.228
have even been financialized.

00:11:11.228 --> 00:11:14.322
Financialized, humility's
not in vogue anymore,

00:11:14.322 --> 00:11:16.059
it's too passive.

00:11:16.059 --> 00:11:17.768
It's a get rich quick on the internet,

00:11:17.768 --> 00:11:20.512
rich is 15 minutes of fame,
world that we live in,

00:11:20.512 --> 00:11:22.354
and we see it every day,

00:11:22.354 --> 00:11:24.586
but, we all want to succeed, right?

00:11:24.586 --> 00:11:26.390
So, the question that we
got to ask ourselves is,

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:30.223
what success is to us,
what success is to you.

00:11:31.313 --> 00:11:32.400
Is it more money?

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:36.293
That's fine, I got nothing against money.

00:11:36.293 --> 00:11:37.126
I don't.

00:11:37.126 --> 00:11:38.603
(audience laughter)

00:11:38.603 --> 00:11:40.504
Maybe it's a healthy family,

00:11:40.504 --> 00:11:42.635
maybe it's a happy marriage,
maybe it's to help others,

00:11:42.635 --> 00:11:45.593
to be famous, to be spiritually sound,

00:11:45.593 --> 00:11:46.426
to leave the world

00:11:46.426 --> 00:11:49.551
a little bit better
place than you found it.

00:11:49.551 --> 00:11:52.368
Continue to ask yourself that question.

00:11:52.368 --> 00:11:55.167
Now, your answer may change
over time, and that's fine,

00:11:55.167 --> 00:11:57.403
but do yourself this favor;

00:11:57.403 --> 00:12:00.215
whatever your answer is,

00:12:00.215 --> 00:12:04.572
don't choose anything that
will jeopardize your soul.

00:12:04.572 --> 00:12:07.698
Prioritize who you are,
who you want to be,

00:12:07.698 --> 00:12:10.212
and don't spend time with anything

00:12:10.212 --> 00:12:13.197
that antagonizes your character.

00:12:13.197 --> 00:12:15.354
Don't drink the Kook Aid, man;

00:12:15.354 --> 00:12:18.304
it tastes sweet, but you
will get cavities tomorrow.

00:12:18.304 --> 00:12:20.921
Alright, life is not a popularity contest.

00:12:20.921 --> 00:12:24.254
Be brave, take the hill, but
first answer that question,

00:12:24.254 --> 00:12:25.504
what's my hill?

00:12:26.916 --> 00:12:30.671
So, me, how do I define success?

00:12:30.671 --> 00:12:32.028
For me, myself.

00:12:32.028 --> 00:12:34.893
Well for me, it's a
measurement of five things.

00:12:34.893 --> 00:12:38.258
We got fatherhood, we
got being a good husband,

00:12:38.258 --> 00:12:40.667
we've got my health,
mind, body, and spirit,

00:12:40.667 --> 00:12:43.452
we got career, and we got friendships.

00:12:43.452 --> 00:12:46.349
These are what's important
to me in my life right now.

00:12:46.349 --> 00:12:48.750
So, I try to measure these
five things each day.

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:50.674
I check in with them, I like to see

00:12:50.674 --> 00:12:53.313
whether or not I'm in
the, the debit section,

00:12:53.313 --> 00:12:54.990
or the credit section, with each one.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:58.522
Am I in the red, or am I
in the black, you follow?

00:12:58.522 --> 00:13:00.848
For instance, sometimes,
say my career's rolling,

00:13:00.848 --> 00:13:02.091
alright, it's way up here in the black,

00:13:02.091 --> 00:13:04.861
but I see how my
relationship with my wife,

00:13:04.861 --> 00:13:07.141
maybe could use a little
bit more of my attention.

00:13:07.141 --> 00:13:09.880
I got to pick up the slack
on being a better husband,

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:12.251
get that one out of the red,

00:13:12.251 --> 00:13:15.546
or say my spiritual health
could use some maintenance.

00:13:15.546 --> 00:13:18.345
It's down here, but hey
man, my friendships,

00:13:18.345 --> 00:13:21.242
and my social life, they're in high gear.

00:13:21.242 --> 00:13:22.755
Right?

00:13:22.755 --> 00:13:24.391
I got to recalibrate.

00:13:24.391 --> 00:13:26.250
Checks and balances,
I got to go to church,

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:29.097
remember to say thank you
more often, something,

00:13:29.097 --> 00:13:31.047
but I got to take the tally,

00:13:31.047 --> 00:13:34.865
because I want to keep
all five in healthy shape,

00:13:34.865 --> 00:13:37.292
and I know that if I
don't take care of them,

00:13:37.292 --> 00:13:40.398
if I don't keep up maintenance on them,

00:13:40.398 --> 00:13:42.943
one of them is going to get weak, man.

00:13:42.943 --> 00:13:45.343
It's going to dip too deep
into the debit section,

00:13:45.343 --> 00:13:48.914
it's going to go bankrupt,
it's going to get sick.

00:13:48.914 --> 00:13:49.747
Die even.

00:13:51.274 --> 00:13:55.133
So first, we have to define
success for ourselves,

00:13:55.133 --> 00:13:57.968
and then, we have to put
in the work to maintain it.

00:13:57.968 --> 00:14:00.534
Take that daily tally, tend our garden,

00:14:00.534 --> 00:14:04.532
keep the things that are
important to us, in good shape.

00:14:04.532 --> 00:14:09.045
Let's admit it, we've
all got two wolves in us;

00:14:09.045 --> 00:14:12.392
a good one, and a bad one,

00:14:12.392 --> 00:14:15.067
and they both want to eat.

00:14:15.067 --> 00:14:17.279
The best I can tell, we just
got to feed that good one

00:14:17.279 --> 00:14:18.592
a little bit more than the other one.

00:14:18.592 --> 00:14:21.121
- One thing I believe, is
it's really important to

00:14:21.121 --> 00:14:23.138
define your own success.

00:14:23.138 --> 00:14:25.597
It's really important
to decide for yourself,

00:14:25.597 --> 00:14:28.147
what success looks like, as
opposed to letting someone else

00:14:28.147 --> 00:14:30.713
impose their definition
of success upon you.

00:14:30.713 --> 00:14:32.319
So, whenever you begin a big project,

00:14:32.319 --> 00:14:34.063
if you're doing something on your own,

00:14:34.063 --> 00:14:35.828
if you're starting a business, or a blog,

00:14:35.828 --> 00:14:37.211
or going back to school, or

00:14:37.211 --> 00:14:39.038
even if it's an exercise
program, whatever it is,

00:14:39.038 --> 00:14:41.595
you know, you should have your
own definition of success.

00:14:41.595 --> 00:14:43.107
- I need to make sure
that everybody knows,

00:14:43.107 --> 00:14:44.509
success is not money.

00:14:44.509 --> 00:14:45.922
Alright, money drives
you up to your problems

00:14:45.922 --> 00:14:47.201
in a limousine, right?

00:14:47.201 --> 00:14:49.520
So, success is sometimes
being a great parent,

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:52.311
a great, dedicating
yourself to your faith.

00:14:52.311 --> 00:14:54.714
There are so many people
that don't necessarily have

00:14:54.714 --> 00:14:55.675
millions, and millions of dollars,

00:14:55.675 --> 00:14:58.214
and they're happier than
many of us ever will be.

00:14:58.214 --> 00:14:59.640
So, I don't want to, you know,

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:01.594
over push the fact of money is success,

00:15:01.594 --> 00:15:02.931
'cause that's not the case.

00:15:02.931 --> 00:15:04.132
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:04.132 --> 00:15:06.182
I'd love to know, what did
you think of this video?

00:15:06.182 --> 00:15:07.937
What clip resonated the most with you?

00:15:07.937 --> 00:15:09.723
What are you going to immediately apply

00:15:09.723 --> 00:15:11.392
to your life, or to your business?

00:15:11.392 --> 00:15:12.824
Leave it down in the comments, below.

00:15:12.824 --> 00:15:14.929
I'm also super-curious, how do you

00:15:14.929 --> 00:15:17.498
define success for yourself?

00:15:17.498 --> 00:15:19.271
What does that look like for you?

00:15:19.271 --> 00:15:21.856
Leave it in the comments, I'm
going to join in the discussion.

00:15:21.856 --> 00:15:23.887
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Blidodi,

00:15:23.887 --> 00:15:26.029
thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:15:26.029 --> 00:15:28.224
Your One Word, and making that fun

00:15:28.224 --> 00:15:30.528
YouTube tribute video, I really, really,

00:15:30.528 --> 00:15:33.165
really appreciate the effort and the love.

00:15:33.165 --> 00:15:36.748
(intense electronic music)

00:15:45.754 --> 00:15:47.553
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:15:47.553 --> 00:15:49.135
I believe in you, I hope you continue

00:15:49.135 --> 00:15:50.549
to believe in yourself,

00:15:50.549 --> 00:15:52.618
and whatever your one word is.

00:15:52.618 --> 00:15:55.035
Much love, I'll see you soon.

